FUN_1000_38bc (key/event poll wait): dropped poll CF -> infinite spin.

asm 0x138bc: store the event mask, then `L: lcall far [DGROUP:0x40a]` (call the frame poll FUN_1000_35a7);
`jb` return when the poll sets CF=1 (frame boundary / empty queue), else `test ax,[dd6a]; je L` loop while
(poll_ax & mask)==0.  Ghidra dropped the x86 CF (uninitialised in_CF local), so the CF=1 early return never
fired and, on the empty-queue intro path where the poll returns ax=0, FUN_1000_38bc spun forever (the intro
player FUN_0000_e584 hung after posting its first frame command).  Thread the poll CF via the shim global
g_fist_cf (set by the reconstructed FUN_1000_35a7, patch 073), same fix class as FUN_1000_38cc (patch 074).
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -44594,25 +44594,29 @@
 
 
